description:
Pre-existing coverage gap, found by the QCLI-523 round-2 full review (unit quest-cli-review-658r2, model deepseek-flash, DEC-183 Stage 1, APPROVE of opum-ai/quest-cli#658 at eba86889) and deliberately NOT fixed in that PR, which reduced only the release check at src/application/tasks/id-allocation.ts:278. The LOCKED-REREAD comparison at src/application/tasks/id-allocation.ts:264-268 (the `current.pid !== holder.pid || current.at !== holder.at` ownership re-check after the break file is taken) has both halves individually unpinned: the only fixture that reaches it with a changed lock is the QCLI-495 round-2 NEW 1 interleaving test at test/qcli495-id-allocation-unit.test.ts:360-414, and its afterStaleJudgement seam at :390-394 replaces the lock with `${process.pid}
${now}
` against a stale `${deadPid}
${now - 60_000}
` -- BOTH halves change at once, so removing either half of the comparison leaves all 17 tests green. This is the same shape the round-1 review of #658 found in the release check, one comparison earlier. Proposed fix: two cases at the afterStaleJudgement seam, each changing exactly one half of the replacement lock. Not to be worked until the day plan names it.
